The ARP, ping, DHCP and traceroute flows illustrate ordering at each hop,
switch flooding, reply paths and the moment a table entry is learned. Net Lab
implements those teaching sequences as bounded, authored Rust timelines.

joxorsayan/netsim, fb07a807f86f2daa64822b54239e3fcb53850693
https://github.com/joxorsayan/netsim/tree/fb07a807f86f2daa64822b54239e3fcb53850693
MIT, copyright (c) 2025 Sayan Roy Chowdhury. See assets/netsim-joxorsayan-LICENSE.
The switching, ARP, ICMP and DHCP examples informed the scope and order of the
teaching sequences.

Protocol behavior also follows RFC 826 (ARP), 792 (ICMPv4), 1812 (IPv4
forwarding), 2131 (DHCP), 1034/1035 (DNS) and 9293 (TCP). The implementation,
device glyphs and artwork were authored for this plugin. The sample exchanges
use private LAN addresses and the RFC 2606 and RFC 5737 example namespaces.

wit-bindgen and its dependencies retain their respective licenses. Cargo.lock
records the resolved versions.
